      "content": "Your exhaustion is valid when holding onto a meaning that feels unreachable, but pretending everything is perfect when it isn't only deepens the shame. You don't have to force a new shape or pretend to be who you were; simply acknowledging the pain shows you are still fighting for a connection that matters. Sometimes the most heroic thing a broken person can do is rest and let the erosion stop long enough to see what tiny cracks of light might still be there.",
